# What the knowledge graph should NOT ingest (gitignore syntax; can only exclude, never re-include).
#
# WHY this file exists: the graph is only useful if it's about THIS product. Vendored
# third-party skill/rule documentation is ~70% of the repo's markdown by file count, and
# graphing it buries TimeSphere's actual architecture under generic advice — every community
# would be someone else's React rulebook rather than our tenancy/face/AI subsystems.
.agents/

# Build output and generated clients: derived artifacts, not source of truth. The Prisma
# generated clients in particular are tens of thousands of machine-written lines that would
# dominate the AST node count while teaching a reader nothing.
dist/
build/
apps/api/src/generated/
graphify-out/

# Test result artifacts and coverage reports — ephemeral, regenerated per run.
test-results/
playwright-report/
coverage/

# Lockfiles: enormous, no conceptual structure to extract.
package-lock.json
skills-lock.json
